# The image is Linux and `COPY` takes the working tree verbatim. Git for
# Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true` in its system config, which checks every
# text file out as CRLF; `docker-entrypoint.sh` then reaches the container with
# a `#!/bin/bash\r` shebang, the kernel looks for an interpreter literally
# named `/bin/bash\r`, and Tini reports `exec linkedin-mcp-entrypoint failed:
# No such file or directory` with exit 127. Pinning LF here is what keeps a
# Windows checkout able to build a working image.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touched, on any platform.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.zip binary
*.mcpb binary
